"P2435285033" "You collected the Snake skin that Matthew Burke requested, but you also found something else. The words of Sithius echo in your head: 'Almighty Stheno.' Who could this creature be?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BookOfStheno 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2522103457" "Book of Stheno"
// DetailString :
"P51355195" "This ancient tome refers to Stheno, the sister of the Gorgon, Medusa. It seems she is the goddess worshipped by Mercy's Snakes. It speaks of a time when Stheno will return to spawn new and powerful progeny."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - HatcheryLoc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2953788395" "The Hatchery's Location"
// DetailString :
"P2242024002" "One of the Snakes you defeated gasped: <br><br>'Leave me be! You will never learn of my lady'sss den from me!' <br><br>After a judicious interrogation, however, the Snake revealed the location of a Snake hatchery."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ShellFragments 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P700535311" "Snake Shell Fragments"
// DetailString :
"P167721627" "You recovered these Snake shell fragments from the Snake hatchery. Though you were unable to find the Gorgon Stheno, these fragments should be worth a lot to Burke's secretive client."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2904150107" "The Origins of the Snakes"
// DetailString :
"P4009599376" "It began with a new client for Matthew Burke. The client wanted information on the nature of the strange Snake creatures who plague Mercy Island, and Jordan had agreed to get it. You went to recover a Snake skin, and came away with some interesting information. The Snakes you fought had referred to a creature called 'almighty Stheno,' and you and Burke resolved to seek it out. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1023117471" "It began with a new client for Matthew Burke. The client wanted information on the nature of the strange Snake creatures who plague Mercy Island, and Burke had agreed to get it. You went to recover a Snake skin, and came away with some interesting information. The Snakes you fought had referred to a creature called 'almighty Stheno,' and you and Burke resolved to seek it out. <br><br> Burke tracked down some rumors, so he sent you to another Snake den. There, you recovered the Book of Stheno, which helped clear up the mystery. Stheno was a Gorgon, the sister of the legendary Medusa. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL1_MI_Burke_MiniArc2_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P194872863" "Snake Shell Fragment"
// tDetailString :
"P3159086953" "You kept this Snake shell fragment from the Snake hatchery you violated in search of Stheno. It's a reminder of your investigation into: <br><br><b>The Origins of the Snakes</b><br><br>It began with a new client for Matthew Burke. The client wanted information on the nature of the strange Snake creatures who plague Mercy Island, and Burke had agreed to get it. You went to recover a Snake skin, and came away with some interesting information. The Snakes you fought had referred to a creature called 'almighty Stheno,' and you and Burke resolved to seek it out. <br><br> Burke tracked down some rumors, so he sent you to another Snake den. There, you recovered the Book of Stheno, which helped clear up the mystery. Stheno was a Gorgon, the sister of the legendary Medusa. <br><br>Burke was determined to track down Stheno himself, if he could. He learned of a Snake hatchery in the area and sent you there. Although you failed to find Stheno herself, you did destroy every egg in the hatchery. So it's a safe bet that Stheno might now be looking for you."

